/// Chapter 37 of the guide, written from md-docs/reference/runtime-api.md by
/// scripts/docsite/guide.py; edit the guide, not this file.
page RuntimeGuide(path: "/reference/runtime", title: "Runtime API", description: "The runtime reference, window.WF: signals, elements, motion, routing, data, stores and their inspection, widgets, safety, text and boot, module by module.", layout: DocsShell("Runtime API", kind: .reference, chapter: t("nav.group.reference"), blurb: "window.WF — the runtime every compiled page calls, usable from a script of your own, the console or a library's callback.", source: "md-docs/reference/runtime-api.md", sections: [Anchor(id: "calling-the-runtime", label: "Calling the runtime"), Anchor(id: "events-the-runtime-dispatches", label: "Events the runtime dispatches"), Anchor(id: "state", label: "State"), Anchor(id: "elements", label: "Elements"), Anchor(id: "bodies", label: "Bodies"), Anchor(id: "keys-focus-and-gestures", label: "Keys, focus and gestures"), Anchor(id: "motion", label: "Motion"), Anchor(id: "routing-and-pages", label: "Routing and pages"), Anchor(id: "browser-values", label: "Browser values"), Anchor(id: "data-and-connections", label: "Data and connections"), Anchor(id: "stores", label: "Stores"), Anchor(id: "widgets-and-layers", label: "Widgets and layers"), Anchor(id: "safety", label: "Safety"), Anchor(id: "text-and-formatting", label: "Text and formatting"), Anchor(id: "values", label: "Values"), Anchor(id: "boot-and-interop", label: "Boot and interop")], prevTo: "/reference/tokens", prevLabel: t("ch.36"), nextTo: "/reference/grammar", nextLabel: t("ch.38"))) {
    Stack(gap: .lg) {
        Markdown("This chapter is the reference for `window.WF`, the runtime every compiled page calls. Look up a function here when a script of your own, a library's callback or the browser's console needs to do what a page does — navigate, show a toast, read a store.\n\n`app.js` opens with the runtime, and the page reaches it as `window.WF`. This plain script, in `src/`, moves to a route, shows a toast and logs what a store holds:")

        CodeBlock(#"// src/support.js
function openHelp() {
  WF.navigate("/about");
  WF.toast("Saved", "success");
  console.log(WF.storeSnapshot("Cart"));
}"#, title: "js")

        Heading("Calling the runtime", id: "calling-the-runtime").h2

        Markdown("These rules apply to every function in this chapter:\n\n- **Who calls it.** The compiled pages call the runtime. So may a project script under `src/` or in `meta.scripts`, a library's callback, or you in the browser's console.\n- **Which functions to call.** Most names here are what the compiler emits for a language feature, listed so you can read the output. The ones meant for your own code are marked **●**.\n- **Modules.** The runtime is a set of feature modules. Each table names the module a function belongs to, and a build ships only the modules its own code reaches. The project's own scripts count: a `WF.toast(…)` in `src/support.js` ships `toast`. Only a call the build cannot see — a name built from a string, a script loaded from another origin — needs `\"build\": \{ \"runtime\": \"full\" \}` ([Call WF from a script](/recipes/call-wf-from-a-script)).")

        Heading("Events the runtime dispatches", id: "events-the-runtime-dispatches").h2

        Markdown("`wf:render` is dispatched on `document` once a drawing lands: the first mount, the takeover of a pre-rendered page, and every route change. Its `detail` is `\{ route, params \}`. A script that finds elements itself listens for it:")

        CodeBlock(#"// src/highlight-tables.js
document.addEventListener("wf:render", (e) => {
  for (const t of document.querySelectorAll("table.sortable")) t.dataset.route = e.detail.route;
});"#, title: "js")

        Markdown("See also: [JavaScript interop](/recipes/listen-for-wf-render).")

        Heading("State", id: "state").h2

        Table(caption: "State") {
            Table.Head {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Function").header
                    Table.Cell("Module").header
                    Table.Cell("What it does").header
                }
            }
            Table.Body {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`signal(value)` ●") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`core`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("A reactive value: call it to read it; `.set(v)`, `.update(f)` and `.subscribe(f)` change and watch it.") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`computed(fn)` ●") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`core`") }
                    Table.Cell("A value computed from signals, recomputed when they change.")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`effect(fn)` ●") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`core`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("Runs `fn`, and again when a signal it read changes. A function `fn` returns is its cleanup, run before the next run and when the effect is disposed. An effect that changes what it reads on every run is stopped after 100 nested runs (with a warning under `wf serve`).") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`scoped(fn)`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`core`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("Runs `fn` in a new scope: what it creates is disposed of with the scope.") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`onCleanup(fn)`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`core`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("Registers `fn` to run when the current scope is disposed.") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`every(ms, fn)`, `after(ms, fn)`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`core`") }
                    Table.Cell("A repeating or one-shot timer that stops with the current scope.")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`listen(target, event, fn, options)`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`core`") }
                    Table.Cell("An event listener removed with the current scope.")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`ref()`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`core`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("An element handle, filled when the element is made; used as the element itself (`name.focus()`, `name.value`).") }
                }
            }
        }

        Heading("Elements", id: "elements").h2

        Table(caption: "Elements") {
            Table.Head {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Function").header
                    Table.Cell("Module").header
                    Table.Cell("What it does").header
                }
            }
            Table.Body {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`el(tag, attrs, …children)`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`core`") }
                    Table.Cell("Makes an element. A function given as an attribute or a child follows the signals it reads.")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`text(fn)`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`core`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("A text node that follows what `fn` reads.") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`props(given, defaults)`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`core`") }
                    Table.Cell("A component's props, with defaults filled in.")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`classes(node, fn)`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`core`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("Live classes: the classes `fn` named last time come off, the ones it names now go on.") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`mark(node, attrs)`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`core`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("Puts `data-wf-exit`, `data-wf-delay`, `data-wf-duration` and `data-wf-animate` on a component's root, for the bodies below to play.") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`rootAttrs(node, attrs)`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`core`") }
                    Table.Cell("Writes the attributes a component call passes onto the component's root element.")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`onRoot(node, event, fn)`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`core`") }
                    Table.Cell("A handler on a component's root element.")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`bound(control)`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`core`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("What a bound control holds, typed: a number field's number (`null` when empty), a select's option value as it was written, otherwise the text.") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`emit(props, event, …args)`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`core`") }
                    Table.Cell("Fires a component's declared event.")
                }
            }
        }

        Heading("Bodies", id: "bodies").h2

        Markdown("What the control-flow statements and slots compile to.")

        Table(caption: "Bodies") {
            Table.Head {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Function").header
                    Table.Cell("Module").header
                    Table.Cell("What it does").header
                }
            }
            Table.Body {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`when(parent, cond, then, else, anim)`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`when`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`if` / `else`.") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`held(read)`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`when`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("What an `if let` binding reads: the value now, or the last one while the branch leaves.") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`each(parent, list, item, options)`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`each`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`for`, keyed or not. Keyed items keep their nodes across inserts, removals and moves, and with `live` across a new value too.") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`show(parent, cond, body, anim)`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`show`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`show`.") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`match(parent, key, arg, arms)`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`match`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`match`. An arm is called with the value and an accessor of it, and drawn again when the arm changes.") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`slot(parent, values, render)`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`slot`") }
                    Table.Cell("A component's slot, drawing the caller's fill.")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`windowed(node, listFn, itemFn, options)`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`windowed`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("A `VirtualList`'s keyed `for`.") }
                }
            }
        }

